  data: {
    LLM: 'Play is anticlockwise. The dealer begins by discarding one card face up. Only the most recently discarded card may be taken. Priority to take the discard: (1) any player who can complete eight pairs and win; (2) any player who can form a Dui (identical pair) with the discard; (3) the player to the right of the discarder, who may take it if no one else does. If you take the discard to form a Dui, place the pair face up in front of you and discard one card; the player to your right plays next. If no one takes the discard, the next player in turn may either take the discard or draw the top card from the stock, then discards one card face up. Play continues until someone has eight pairs and wins.',
    Player: 'Play is anticlockwise. The dealer begins by discarding one card face up. Only the most recently discarded card may be taken. Priority to take the discard: (1) any player who can complete eight pairs and win; (2) any player who can form a Dui (identical pair) with the discard; (3) the player to the right of the discarder, who may take it if no one else does. If you take the discard to form a Dui, place the pair face up in front of you and discard one card; the player to your right plays next. If no one takes the discard, the next player in turn may either take the discard or draw the top card from the stock, then discards one card face up. Play continues until someone has eight pairs and wins.',
    objective: 'The object is to collect a 16-card hand consisting of eight pairs (dui or ka). The first player to do so exposes their cards and wins the agreed stake from each opponent; if all eight pairs are identical (dui), the winner collects double stake (quan dui).',
    gameplay: 'Play is anticlockwise. The dealer begins by discarding one card face up. Only the most recently discarded card may be taken. Priority to take the discard: (1) any player who can complete eight pairs and win; (2) any player who can form a Dui (identical pair) with the discard; (3) the player to the right of the discarder, who may take it if no one else does. If you take the discard to form a Dui, place the pair face up in front of you and discard one card; the player to your right plays next. If no one takes the discard, the next player in turn may either take the discard or draw the top card from the stock, then discards one card face up. Play continues until someone has eight pairs and wins.',
    keyRules: [
      'Dui is a pair of identical cards; Ka is a pair of same number in different suits. The three odd cards count as ones. Completing eight pairs wins; all eight Dui (quan dui) pays double stake. Winner may optionally continue playing for quan dui instead of claiming with mixed Ka and Dui, unless the final pair was claimed from the discard as Ka.',
    ],
